# M31. The left arm loses its 12 V for 300 ms while holding, with no stop-sense edge (a loose plug). Its servos
# reboot with torque off and their torque limit reset. Read before act: the coordinator latches feedback_stale
# while they are silent, and once they answer it reads torque off and the limit not the one it wrote. After the
# clear it writes no goal to them (a goal could turn torque on), and a pose is refused until torque is turned
# on again from the terminal with Confirm.
expect motion mode ready
key torque-on-left
wait 2100
key c
expect motion torque left on
key power-cycle-left
expect motion fault feedback_stale arm_left
expect sim left follower power back
wait 300
key operator-clear
wait 2100
key c
expect motion cleared all faults
expect motion torque left follower off (re-read)
absent 1000 sim torque-on
key pose-ready-left
expect motion command arm.go_to_pose refused:torque_off operator_cli
key inspect-goals-left
absent 500 sim goal-write left follower
key q
